{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T05:13:03.902Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"72bc6070cdf8e143b3ffadf4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-xcndcu"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A time-bounded gate waiver expires straight into a release block: no notice window, and the gate's text output names neither the item nor the expiry"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-12 by the daily release-health check. The 03:45Z morning dispatcher run 43150266775 failed at static-quality-gate and opened GH-1709. The blocking assertion was repository-defect-evidence-required: the closed defect pm-m1tfmp carries an explicit_waiver whose waiver_expires_at (2026-11-12T00:00:00Z) passed at midnight UTC. Nothing in the repository changed; the calendar crossed a date the tracker had recorded for a month.\n\nThree problems. (1) No notice window: a waiver is valid until the second it expires and then blocks every release, pull request and nightly at once, with no earlier signal on any channel an agent reads. (2) The gate's text output, which is what the release log keeps, says only 'Findings: 1'. The failure record names neither the item nor the reason, so recovery needed a local --json rerun. (3) The same cliff repeats across the population: four boundary-fixture waivers in config/boundary-fixtures.json expire 2026-11-16 and three CodeQL disposition waivers (pm-codeql48, pm-codeql49, pm-codeql4849) expire 2026-11-21, so the release would have blocked again on both days.\n\nA census of every dated waiver in the repository found 32 surface-replication waivers. The 8 with future dates are scoped to the unchanged check, which diffs against the default-branch base and so binds only at pull-request time; they cannot block a release on main. The release-blocking population is therefore exactly the defect-evidence gate: item gate_evidence waivers plus boundary-fixture waivers."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["defect-evidence","governance","quality-gate","release","reliability","waivers"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-12T05:13:03.902Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-12T05:13:03.902Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The SDK defect-evidence and boundary-fixture evaluators report every waiver expiring inside a declared notice window (subject, owner, expiry, days remaining) without failing the release gate; The notice window is declared as data in the recurrence policy and validated when the policy is parsed; A scheduled assurance gate fails when any waiver is inside the notice window, so the existing nightly alert opens an issue before the waiver can block a release; The gate's text output names every finding and every waiver inside the notice window; Negative controls prove the notice gate fails for a waiver inside the window and passes for one outside it"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-1jzupz"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A waiver approaching expiry raises a nightly alert days ahead and is renewed or retired through a reviewed change before it can block a release"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"pm-m1tfmp's waiver expired at 00:00Z on 2026-11-12 and the next release gate failed with 'Findings: 1' and no earlier signal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-0pzgit","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:03.902Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-7zs0","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:03.902Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-codeql48","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:03.902Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-codeql4849","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:03.902Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-codeql49","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:03.902Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-m1tfmp","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:03.902Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-rtn5h6","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:03.902Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"14cad8cd30ac39adb5cf5b8e07f0253fea834e6f52d8241d0396599f70491cc5","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"06df11ac17c864cfeea5cb0bb86e307fdea5ee406fb62c030c36f502e8a9117a"}
